          #InjectivityOfPullbackInCohomologyToBT.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              One way to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B i^*\colon H^*(B G) \to H^*(B T)
              is injective is by using
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
              to recognise that this map is just
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sym
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Sym
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔱
                      %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym^{\ast} \mathfrak{g}^{\vee} \to Sym^{\ast} \mathfrak{t}^{\vee}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a compact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %p
              One can define a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Becker-Gottlieb+transfer"} transfer map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau\colon H^*(B T) \to H^*(B G)
              as in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/61784/cohomology-of-bg-g-compact-lie-group/61943#61943"} this MO answer
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Dupont78"} Dupont 1978
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau\circ B i^*\colon H^*(B G)\to H^*(B G)
              is multiplication by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+class"} Euler class
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
